# IntellyRouter runtime environment.
#
# Copy to .env and edit, then pass `--env-file .env` to docker compose or
# use the Variables section on Dokploy / Coolify.

# Where the gateway listens. Dokploy / Coolify must publish the container
# port (7117) and front it with TLS; the gateway does not terminate TLS.
INTELLYROUTER_ADDR=0.0.0.0:7117

# Data directory. Mapped to a persistent volume so master.key and the
# SQLite database survive restarts.
INTELLYROUTER_DATA=/data

# Eval task directory.
INTELLYROUTER_EVAL_TASKS=/eval-tasks

# Where the host publishes the container port. Loopback by default, so a
# fresh deploy is not exposed. Set a LAN or tailnet address to reach the
# gateway from other machines, or 0.0.0.0:7117 behind a reverse proxy that
# terminates TLS. The gateway does not terminate TLS itself.
# INTELLYROUTER_PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:7117

# Where Claude Code inside the container finds its config and credentials.
# The image ships Claude Code; the persistent volume at /data holds its
# config and login so they survive restarts and image rebuilds.
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/data/.claude

# Pick ONE (or both) of the login paths below. Leave both commented if
# you only use API-key providers and don't run a Claude-Code director or
# the eval runner.
#
# (A) HEADLESS — host runs `claude setup-token` once, paste the printed
# value here. Token lasts ~1 year; works for container-originated
# subscription calls. The command is interactive (opens a browser on
# the operator's laptop, not the server).
#
#   $ claude setup-token
#   sk-ant-oat01-...
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
#
# (B) INTERACTIVE — `docker compose exec intellyrouter claude auth login`
# from the host. Device-code flow; paste the code at claude.ai/device.
# Credentials land in /data/.claude/.credentials.json on the volume and
# survive restarts.
#
# Skip this section entirely if you only use API-key providers and don't
# run the eval runner or a Claude-Code director.

# IMPORTANT — what does NOT work in a container:
#
# The gateway relays subscription traffic end-to-end, so subscription
# routes work in a container. What does not work is the parts of the
# gateway that originate their own subscription calls when no Claude
# Code login is present and no API-key provider is configured. The
# following need either `claude` on PATH + a login, or an API-key
# provider:
#
#  - The Claude-Code director (DirectorSettings.ClaudeCode: true).
#  - The subscription advisor.
#  - The eval runner (`intelly-eval`).
#
# Everything else (subscription passthrough, API-key directors, advisor
# on API-key models, classifier, escalation tiers, combos) is fine inside
# a container.
